  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}). No pair verb.\n\nUSAGE:\nぼやく is often used for everyday, minor complaints expressed in a muttering or grumbling tone. It's less formal than {文句|もんく}を{言|い}う and implies a certain resignation or lack of expectation that the complaint will be addressed.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・〜とぼやく (to grumble that ~)\n・〜についてぼやく (to grumble about ~)\n・ぼやきながら (while grumbling)\n\nREGISTER:\nCasual to neutral. Often used in everyday conversation.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・{愚痴|ぐち}をこぼす - to complain/vent (more about emotional release)\n・{文句|もんく}を{言|い}う - to complain (more direct, stronger)\n・つぶやく - to mutter (neutral, not necessarily complaining)",
